  "notes": "Modified cash basis village; treated as cash basis. Governmental columns from p5 Total Governmental Funds; beginning/ending cash = total fund balances (cash, CDs, county treasurer cash). Taxes 94,042 split into property 64,708 and sales tax 29,334 per the Statement of Activities (p2), tying to General Fund and LB 840 Fund columns. Intergovernmental - other 126,025: Homestead exemption 9,754 split out using the p12 General Fund combining schedule; the remainder 116,271 (Street Fund 76,375 with no breakdown + equalization 35,134 + other state and federal 4,762) stays state aid. Roll-forward: 663,328 + 861,074 - 911,909 + 158,920 - 158,920 = 612,493. Business-type from p8 proprietary Total column (Water, Sewer, Sanitation); measure net position; totals computed (operating + nonoperating); 2,078,294 + 225,308 - 305,922 = 1,997,680. Proprietary cash-flow statement is modified cash basis, so proprietary null. Balance sheet: government-wide Statement of Net Position (includes capital assets and business-type debt). Detail: p12-13 General Fund combining schedule (6 sub-fund columns), p14 nonmajor combining (LB 840, ARPA, Housing Rehabilitation); p11 all-funds budget schedule used only for Street Fund (Streets and Highways) and business-type lines (Sanitation, Wastewater, Water, debt principal/interest); its revenue lines and the Keno Fund (community development 8,121, keno revenues 68,791, interest 1,048) are mixed across funds and not recorded; Street Fund revenues have no separate schedule. Transfer cross-check: Street in 32,920 = ARPA out 32,920; General in/out 63,000 and Keno in/out 63,000 offset (158,920 each way); no hidden transfers. Read pages 1-14 of 14"
}
